# Iris Emulator

Read `docs/PRD.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `docs/ROADMAP.md` before changing architecture.

- Implement one milestone at a time. Milestone 5 (integer scaling, aspect ratio, fullscreen, and presentation shaders) is implemented. Do not start later milestones: the game library or other consoles.
- The emulation core must not include SDL window types, ImGui, or Win32 UI types. Desktop code calls services and does not read CPU or PPU internals.
- Do not add menu items, settings, or buttons that do not work.
- Do not add commercial ROMs, proprietary firmware, copied UI assets, or a copy of Tahoma.
- Keep third-party libraries pinned. Do not change a dependency or its license silently.
- Presentation filters must not modify emulated PPU output.

```cpp
// Do not do this. Desktop code does not touch CPU state.
cpu.registers().pc = 0x8000;

// Do this. Desktop code asks the system interface.
system->reset();
```
